## portus.query — lectura del query string (`?a=1&b=2`).
##
## Decodifica porcentajes y `+` como espacio (form encoding) y devuelve pares
## en orden de aparición. Los nombres repetidos se conservan.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## var query as portus.query.Query is calling portus.query.parse_query with "a=1&b=hola+mundo"
## let a as maybe string is calling portus.query.query_get with query, "a"
## ```
##
## ## Memoria
## `parse_query` devuelve un valor con memoria propia; libéralo con
## `free_query` (o `query_drop` si solo la usaste).
import std.cipher
import std.scrolls
import std.ward
import portus.text

## Un par nombre/valor del query string.
rune QueryPair:
    ## Nombre ya decodificado.
    name as string
    ## Valor ya decodificado.
    value as string

## El query string de una petición, en orden.
rune Query:
    ## Pares en el orden en que llegaron.
    pairs as list of QueryPair

## Decodifica `raw` (`a=1&b=2`) en pares.
##
## Un par sin `=` se guarda con valor `""`. Un porcentaje inválido deja el
## texto tal cual (no falla la petición entera).
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve un valor propio; libéralo con `free_query`.
weave parse_query with raw as string into Query:
    var pairs as list of QueryPair is []
    if raw.len == 0:
        return with pairs is pairs
    var parts as list of string is calling scrolls.split with raw, "&"
    var i as int is 0
    while i < parts.len:
        var part as string is (parts at i)
        if part.len > 0:
            var eq as int is calling scrolls.index_of with part, "="
            var name_raw as string is ""
            var value_raw as string is ""
            if eq < 0:
                set name_raw is part
            else:
                set name_raw is calling scrolls.substring with part, 0, eq
                set value_raw is calling scrolls.substring with part, eq + 1, part.len
            var name as string is calling _decode with name_raw
            var value as string is calling _decode with value_raw
            if eq >= 0:
                banish value_raw
            banish name_raw
            calling pairs.push with with name is name, value is value
        set i is i + 1
    calling text.free_strings with parts
    return with pairs is pairs

## Primer valor de `name`, o `none`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Copia propia; libérala o pásala a `banish`.
weave query_get with query as Query, name as string into maybe string:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < query.pairs.len:
        var pair as QueryPair is (query.pairs at i)
        if (calling scrolls.compare with pair.name, name) == 0:
            return some (calling scrolls.substring with pair.value, 0, pair.value.len)
        set i is i + 1
    return maybe none

## `true` si el query string trae `name`.
weave query_has with query as Query, name as string into bool:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < query.pairs.len:
        var pair as QueryPair is (query.pairs at i)
        if (calling scrolls.compare with pair.name, name) == 0:
            return true
        set i is i + 1
    return false

## Libera el query string y todos sus pares.
weave free_query with query as Query into void:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < query.pairs.len:
        var pair as QueryPair is (query.pairs at i)
        banish pair.name
        banish pair.value
        set i is i + 1
    banish query.pairs

## Decodifica un componente (`%20`, `+` como espacio).
##
## Nunca falla: si el porcentaje es inválido devuelve una copia tal cual.
weave _decode with raw as string into string:
    if raw.len == 0:
        return ""
    var plus_fixed as string is calling scrolls.replace_all with raw, "+", " "
    var decoded as maybe string is calling cipher.decode_url with plus_fixed
    banish plus_fixed
    if v as string is decoded:
        # El maybe es dueño del payload: se copia antes de liberar la caja.
        var out as string is "{v}"
        banish decoded
        return out
    banish decoded
    return calling scrolls.substring with raw, 0, raw.len

test "parse_query decodifica y conserva el orden":
    var q as Query is calling parse_query with "a=1&b=hola+mundo&c=%C3%A9"
    calling ward.assert_eq_int with q.pairs.len, 3
    let a as maybe string is calling query_get with q, "a"
    calling ward.assert_eq_string with (a or else "?"), "1"
    let b as maybe string is calling query_get with q, "b"
    calling ward.assert_eq_string with (b or else "?"), "hola mundo"
    calling free_query with q

test "parse_query acepta un par sin igual":
    var q as Query is calling parse_query with "flag&x=2"
    let v as maybe string is calling query_get with q, "flag"
    calling ward.assert_eq_string with (v or else "?"), ""
    calling ward.assert_true with (calling query_has with q, "x")
    calling free_query with q
